# J45 — Map WORKLIST section: frame + plain parity (P5)  ⭐ release-blocking
#
# Keyless, deterministic. The Map page carries a WORKLIST divider (top-5 risk-ranked
# files + the "run worklist for all N" affordance). The divider is part of the Map
# layout, so it renders whether or not a threshold-crossing file exists. Frame parity
# uses the phase fixture (demo target); plain parity uses the SEPARATE map plain
# projection (map.rs plain_lines — the plan warns Map plain parity is not automatic).
name: the Map WORKLIST section renders in both the frame and the plain projection
size: 120x40
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 RUN FOCUS
keys: b
wait-for: 30 findings / 1 crit
wait: 2
submit: workbench
wait: 2
nav-mode:
keys: 1
wait-live-snap: 12 Viewing Map | map-worklist
expect: WORKLIST
ask: The Map WORKLIST section is present as its own divider; when rows exist they are top-5, one line each, with the "run worklist for all N" affordance and no citation truncated into ambiguity.
# Exit the TUI (Navigate mode on a workbench page — idle Ctrl+C exits).
keys: C-c
wait: 3
# Plain parity: the map plain projection is a SEPARATE code path; assert the
# WORKLIST divider survives style-stripping in non-TTY output.
launch-raw: printf 'workbench\nquit\n' | @KUZUSHI --target @TMP_TARGET 2>&1 | grep -iE 'WORKLIST'
wait: 5
snap: map-worklist-plain
expect: WORKLIST
ask: The WORKLIST divider appears in the plain (non-TTY) Map projection with no ANSI / box-drawing dependency — provenance is not color-only.
